 and leisure as well as being  directly involved in a handful of other  companies all focused on next-generation  technologies that Matthews believes will  give him his next  big success by following his passion am  I not giving up at the first sign of  failure Terry Matthews was able to go  from having to borrow $4,000 to start up  a business into becoming a billionaire  to help grow your business  here are three auction items that you  can learn from Terry Matthews auction  item number one be persistent if there  were rules of entrepreneurship being  persistent would be close to the top of  the list being an entrepreneur is tough  the people will reject you you're run  short of money you leave in wonder if  you're better to just give up and go get  a nine-to-five job if you have a passion  for what you do and you're providing a  valuable service or product to your  customers you have to keep going remind  yourself why you started your business  and hold on to the image of you being  the successful entrepreneur that you  want to be it's a long tough road but  it's totally worth it be persistent and  keep going  Matthews career has largely been  characterized by two things is for  sensitive and active involvement in all  of his companies and his thorough  knowledge of the industry in which is  involved Matthew started 80 different  companies and has an excellent track  record of success he is a hands-on  investor and persistent when it comes to  business when he first started out he  discovered when you leave things to  other people you stand a better chance  of losing money  I've been persistent you can keep  reminding others that you have a good  idea but being hands-on you will not be  a passive investor and will know  everything about the business being able  to solve challenges as they come up  according to Matthews I don't think I'm  stubborn I just focus on the task at  hand and do what it takes persistence is  the single most important thing for  success our