ing to how  much value you're giving your clients if  you're helping solve a major problem for  them and you're providing outstanding  value you can charge more money if  you're an average company sell an  average product don't expect to get  outstanding results keep focused on your  customer and give them the most value  you can think of and they'll reward you  with money in your pocket the bottom  line for Matthews is developing a  product that will in turn deliver real  benefits to his clients under Matthews  leadership  Mitel introduced a product called your  assistant which won accolades across the  board precisely because of its unique  added value  demonstrating valued clients is one of  the biggest challenges companies face  Matthews has reached new heights of  success because he has not just pushed  new technologies he's created products  that opened new opportunities and  offered added value to companies by  focusing on the end results he's been  able to stay at the forefront of the  industry and always one step ahead of  the rest according to Matthews to start  you're not looking at the replacement of  simple things so for example if I said  to a businessperson I have really good  news I'm speaking to you through a voice  over IP system well big deal I can do  that over traditional phones to the  network every different vertical has its  own set of killer apps but the important  thing is that IP broadband has created a  killer environment for new apps during  2004 the conditions that would allow  getting killer apps were there but the  confusion as to how to get there and  what they could gain was not present  companies want to see benefits in a  substantive way anything you can  introduce that one speaks to revenue  growth and to reduces costs and improve  customer satisfaction that's all good  so remember be persistent build  relationships and make your product  beneficial to finish up this video I  wanted to share with my favorite true  stories of Elle